<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>SQLMan</title>
    {% include "component/head.njk" %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style/reset.css"/>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style/home.css"/>
  </head>
  <body class="home-page">
    {% include "component/top.njk" %}
    <main class="content main">
      <section class="design-philosophy" id="features" aria-labelledby="philosophy-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">Built for direct database work</span>
          <h1 id="philosophy-title">Design Philosophy</h1>
          <p>A focused toolkit for teams who want SQL to stay visible, predictable, and fast.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h3>Small/Restraint</h3>
            <p>Simple philosophy, easy to understand the whole package quickly. Minimal introduction of third-party dependencies.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h3>Carefully Designed API</h3>
            <p>Elegant API invocation, reuse of common concepts, consistent usage, and reduced learning curve.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h3>Fast</h3>
            <p>Minimal object creation, efficient database operations. No magic behind the scenes, straightforward execution</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
            <h3>Open</h3>
            <p>100% Open Source with full documentation, commments, unit tests. Community-driven development.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="positioning" aria-label="SqlMan capabilities and boundaries">
        <article class="details-panel advantages">
          <span class="eyebrow">Why SqlMan</span>
          <h2>Some of the advantages of using SqlMan are:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Familiar way for you:
              <ul>
                <li><code>sql().input('SELECT * FROM table WHERE id=?', 1).query()</code></li>
                <li>Multiple lines of SQL written in XML</li>
                <li><code>@Insert</code>, <code>@Update</code>, <code>@Delete</code>, <code>@Query</code> annotations</li>
                <li>Automatically populate JavaBean properties from ResultSets.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Core philosophy centers around SQL. Enhanced SQL logic, supporting dynamic SQL (IF/ForEach).</li>
            <li>Built-in common CRUD/Paging functionality.</li>
            <li>Offers a rich set of extension features.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <aside class="details-panel not-for" aria-labelledby="not-title">
          <span class="eyebrow">Clear boundaries</span>
          <h2 id="not-title">SqlMan is NOT:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>An Object/Relational bridge.</li>
            <li>Does not provide a functional-style chained call.</li>
            <li>A heavyweight framework of any kind.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </section>
      <section class="source-code" aria-labelledby="source-title">
        <span class="eyebrow">Open source</span>
        <h2 id="source-title">Source Code</h2>
        <p>Under GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE v3.0.</p>
        <div class="source-links primary-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/lightweight-component/SqlMan">Github <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="https://gitcode.com/lightweight-component/SqlMan">Gitcode <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="source-links secondary-links">
          <a href="https://sqlman.ajaxjs.com">Website</a>
          <a href="https://sqlman.ajaxjs.com/docs">Documents</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/lightweight-component/SqlMan">JavaDoc</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    {% include "component/footer.njk" %}
  </body>
</html>
